Title: AETHEL: THE LAST HORIZON
Credit: A Feature Screenplay
Genre: Epic Thriller / Survival Action
Draft date: 17 August 2026

FADE IN:

.BLACK #1#

No music.

A LOW NOTE emerges at the edge of hearing.

It deepens until it becomes pressure. Until we feel it in our teeth.

A woman whispers in the dark.

EIRA (V.O.)  
One breath is weather. Two are coincidence. Three are information.

A STONE STRIKES somewhere impossibly far away.

Seven measured breaths.

An echo returns.

Too early.

CUT TO:

INT. THIRD LISTENING VAULT, ORUN — NIGHT #2#

A copper lamp flame leans west.

EIRA SEN, 29, pale and severe in plain reindeer wool, presses one hand to a black basalt pillar. Her other hand hovers over a clay tablet.

She counts under her breath.

EIRA  
Seven... eight—

The echo moves through the pillar.

Eira opens her eyes.

Above her, DRUMS begin. Dust falls. Six hundred feet strike the city floor in rhythm as a concert starts overhead.

The pillar vibrates with music. The impossible echo is gone.

Eira resets a simple signal device: suspended weight, copper plate, braided cord.

She pulls.

Through a slit window, signal lamps flash tower to tower across the night glacier.

Eira waits.

The answering strike comes.

Seven breaths.

Then the drums THUNDER. Human rhythm swallows the ice.

Eira pulls her hand back, frustrated.

The iron door opens. VAR SEN, 26, handsome in an expensive seal-hide coat, carries two cups of hot berry wine.

VAR  
You missed Father’s opening.

EIRA  
I heard it through six ceilings and a controlled test.

VAR  
He’ll be touched.

He gives her a cup, sees her expression.

VAR (CONT'D)  
What?

EIRA  
The western echo arrived early.

VAR  
How early?

EIRA  
Two breaths.

VAR  
I don’t know what that means.

EIRA  
Sound travels faster through water than broken ice.

Var looks down at the floor.

VAR  
There’s always water under ice.

EIRA  
Channels. Not a body.

VAR  
How large a body?

EIRA  
There is no body. There is one bad reading.

She scratches: TRIAL SPOILED BY SURFACE VIBRATION.

Var presses his thumb into the corner of the clay.

EIRA (CONT'D)  
What are you doing?

VAR  
First witness. You heard something before you convinced yourself you didn’t.

Every lamp in the vault LEANS WEST.

The wine trembles.

A DEEP NOTE enters through the floor. The tablet creeps toward the table’s edge.

Above, the concert audience ERUPTS in applause.

They think it was part of the music.

Eira marks the clay so hard her stylus snaps.

TITLE:

> AETHEL: THE LAST HORIZON <

INT. HALL OF NAMES, ORUN — LATER #3#

The audience disperses through towering basalt arches, flushed and tearful.

PELL ORRO, 56, silver at the temples, receives their gratitude. He is Eira and Var’s father, a stone musician who knows exactly how humble genius should look.

Eira waits until they are alone.

EIRA  
Your last note. Was it buried?

PELL  
My last note was silence.

EIRA  
Did you open the north resonator after the foot sequence?

PELL  
Yes.

EIRA  
East chamber?

PELL  
Yes.

EIRA  
Any secondary weight below the hall?

Pell’s warmth closes.

PELL  
No.

EIRA  
You’re certain?

PELL  
Must you turn everything I make into one of her tests?

The absence of a name fills the hall: Eira’s dead mother.

EIRA  
This is not about Mother.

PELL  
Everything between us is about your mother.

He walks away.

Eira stands beneath the arches, tablet in hand.

Far below, the note continues.

SMASH CUT TO:

EXT. LAKE ARUUN — DAWN #4#

Absolute silver.

A freshwater sea with no opposite shore. Reed islands float under wheeling cranes.

SELI NAV, 19, lithe, fierce, crouches in a narrow reed canoe beside a clay route marker.

The marker stands knee-deep in water.

Seli studies the distant shore. The old waterline is high on a willow trunk — but the present shore has withdrawn twelve boat-lengths.

High water and low water at once.

TEM NAV, 48, broad and warm-faced, approaches in a larger boat with two apprentices.

TEM  
You missed first meal.

SELI  
The shore moved.

TEM  
Stones move. Shores are where they are.

She points to her handprint fired into the marker below water.

SELI  
You placed it four lengths inland.

Tem’s smile becomes careful.

TEM  
Wind pressure from the northern bays.

SELI  
No east wind for six days.

TEM  
Southern reeds drinking the basin.

SELI  
Reeds don’t drink twelve boat-lengths before breakfast.

One apprentice laughs.

Tem touches the water.

A lower current runs NORTH beneath a surface current moving SOUTH.

Seli’s face changes. In her mind, the currents become two translucent sheets folding against each other.

SELI (CONT'D)  
The lake is folding.

TEM  
That is not a measurement.

A STURGEON longer than Seli’s canoe surfaces beside them.

Then another.

Five ancient fish roll north through the shallows.

SELI  
They’re ninety days early.

Tem watches the last ring close.

For the first time, he is afraid.

INT. UNDERGROUND GARDEN, TAVRA — MORNING #5#

Copper mirrors carry sunlight down into a black volcanic cavern.

Terraces glow with orange trees, silver moss, black barley and fern. Water whispers through narrow stone channels.

NARA VED, 34, strong and inward, lies in mud with one arm buried under a root ledge.

She draws out a BLACKENED ROOT.

MELE OSSA, 15, thin and defiant, crouches nearby with a basket of obviously stolen medicine jars.

MELE  
Rot?

NARA  
Roots rot from drowning.

MELE  
Everything here is wet.

NARA  
Wet is not drowned.

Nara cuts the root. Grey flesh.

She touches it to her tongue.

Salt.

MELE  
You licked rot.

NARA  
Yes.

MELE  
Was it useful?

NARA  
Yes.

Mele tries to taste it. Nara catches her wrist.

NARA (CONT'D)  
Useful once.

CHIEF GARDENER OSSA, 61, descends with two assessors.

Nara holds out the root.

NARA (CONT'D)  
Taste it.

OSSA  
What am I tasting for?

NARA  
The sea.

The sea lies beyond three ridges and far below.

Ossa smells the root but will not taste it.

OSSA  
Burn the tree.

NARA  
Salt isn’t contagious.

OSSA  
A First Accord delegation arrives in nineteen days. If we close the western gardens, every negotiation begins with our weakness.

NARA  
The tree doesn’t know about the Accord.

OSSA  
That is why people govern trees.

She turns to the assessors.

OSSA (CONT'D)  
Terrace Nine exceeds projected health. Record it.

Nara stares at her.

At midday, the orange tree burns. Its living blossoms fill the cavern with fragrance.

EXT. WIND STEPPE — DAWN #6#

A hundred WOOLLY MAMMOTHS move east in silence.

ORU THE ROADLESS, 48, patient and weathered, watches from beside wheeled hide homes.

His wife SENA joins him.

ORU  
The warm springs are west.

SENA  
Tell them.

Saiga antelope race east. Reindeer move east. Birds rise from western grass.

Oru presses a palm to a glacial boulder.

It trembles.

KORUN BALE, 62, an old Oruni hunter, emerges dragging a sled of clay track casts.

KORUN  
Seven cave lions. Moving east.

ORU  
What are they leaving?

KORUN  
The western shelf.

ORU  
Your city knows?

KORUN  
My city has listeners.

ORU  
They listen to stone.

Korun looks at the departing animals.

KORUN  
That is the problem.

The Roadless turn their wagons east.

Oru mounts a small steppe horse and rides west, alone.

INT. COMMUNAL COURT, TAVRA — NIGHT #7#

A long copper table reflects food, fire and a hundred faces.

ILYON SARR, 42, graceful and magnetic, enters late. People touch him, call his name. He remembers theirs.

His husband BEREN, 40s, broad and flour-dusted, puts a barley cake on his plate.

BEREN  
The Voice has arrived. Hide all simple questions.

Laughter.

Ilyon kisses his temple and sits opposite Nara.

ILYON  
Chief Gardener Ossa reports excellent western yield.

Nara’s expression tells him otherwise.

NARA  
She reported that today?

ILYON  
You disagree?

NARA  
A dead tree is green for several days. Its leaves haven’t learned yet.

Ilyon stops eating.

ILYON  
Orun lost a western listening station.

The court remains warm, loud, alive.

Nara looks at the doubled faces in copper.

NARA  
Do they know why?

ILYON  
They are attentive.

NARA  
That is not the same as afraid.

ILYON  
No.

He worries the edge of his copper wrist band.

ILYON (CONT'D)  
It is what leaders say instead.

EXT. REED MARGIN VILLAGE — PRE-DAWN #8#

Rain taps lightly on roof mats.

KES LUMA, 11, wakes in a stilt house.

The frogs have stopped singing.

Water moves across the floor.

Kes opens the door.

Canoes float level with the threshold. Beyond, an entire marsh village is silently drowning.

A storage tower COLLAPSES.

GRANDMOTHER ISHA, 70s, tears down a partition.

ISHA  
Wake Seliya. Take the map basket.

KES  
Where did the water come from?

ISHA  
All water comes from somewhere. Move.

They push a canoe through the doorway. Children crowd roofs. Goats swim between houses. No storm. No wind.

Isha loads children until the canoe sits one finger above water.

On the open channel, SUUN PATROL BOATS appear through rain, blue sails marked with Maru’s three bars.

Everyone shouts.

One boat turns toward them.

A HORN sounds farther out.

The boat stops.

A voice through a speaking cone:

PATROL VOICE  
Water sickness in the margin. Eastern harbour is closed. Proceed north.

VILLAGER  
There is no north channel!

The boats turn away.

Kes stands dangerously in the canoe.

KES  
We’re here! We’re right here!

A western current slams the canoe sideways.

It capsizes.

Under brown water: limbs, bubbles, map pieces.

Kes surfaces holding the basket. Isha clings to a roof beam with a small boy.

ISHA  
Take him!

The current pulls her toward submerged willows.

She looks at Kes.

ISHA (CONT'D)  
Keep the country.

The willows close around her.

EXT. EASTERN HARBOUR, SUUN — DAY #9#

Forty-one survivors huddle in rain.

MARU DRENN, 51, controlled and imposing, stands with guards and a clerk.

MARU  
Which settlement?

SELIYA  
South Reed.

The clerk checks a tablet.

CLERK  
No registered settlement.

Kes opens the basket. Broken clay maps. Tangled route cords.

KES  
It’s here.

MARU  
Family route marks aren’t civic maps. The margin shifts.

KES  
Our village didn’t.

The clerk presses a tablet.

CLERK  
Forty-one temporary dependents. Origin: unoccupied wetland.

Kes knocks the tablet down and STAMPS it.

KES  
It was not empty!

A guard grabs him. Maru raises a hand. Release him.

MARU  
What should we write?

Kes gives the true name — long, musical, untranslatable.

CLERK  
There isn’t space.

KES  
Use another tablet.

Maru studies him.

MARU  
Write the name.

The clerk starts again.

Kes gathers his broken country and walks past Maru without thanks.

EXT. TAVRA — DAY #10#

The Ember Coast in full splendour.

Basalt terraces descend toward a shining western sea. Copper light towers catch the sun. Waterfalls thread through laurel forest. Great elephants move among distant trees.

Delegations converge on the city:

— Oruni sleds carrying a block of blue ice.

— Suun reed craft climbing the river under indigo sails.

— Kheledi riders in pale linen and ochre.

— Marsh survivors walking behind everyone else.

MARA-OF-NO-HEARTH, 36, patched in the colours of all four cultures, sings beside the road.

MARA (V.O.)  
Four peoples came carrying four waters. None knew the fifth had arrived before them.

INT. COPPER HALL, TAVRA — DAY #11#

Eighty-three delegates surround an empty copper table.

AVEN TAL, 40, a Kheledi mediator, stands between four bowls: glacial ice, lake water, spring water, half a cup from a drought cistern.

AVEN  
Fear is weather within the body. It requires no permission. We are here to determine what obligations evidence creates between us.

RUSK VEY, 58, First Speaker of Orun, nods to Eira.

She stands, uncomfortable under attention.

EIRA  
The western echo indicates either a new cavity beneath the shelf or a large body of water reversing the basal channels.

DELEGATE  
How large?

EIRA  
Unknown.

DELEGATE  
When does it reach inhabited ground?

EIRA  
Unknown.

SIMO VARR, 27, Ilyon’s ambitious protégé, leans forward.

SIMO  
What do you know?

EIRA  
That anyone promising certainty is lying.

Uneasy reactions.

Tem rises among Suun delegates.

TEM  
My household found divided water on the eastern basin.

Seli looks at him: *Your household?*

AVEN  
Who observed it?

A beat.

TEM  
My daughter.

Seli comes to the table. She folds two pieces of cloth against each other.

SELI  
The lake is moving north below and south above. Rising here. Withdrawing here. It’s folding.

Some delegates smile at the metaphor.

Eira does not.

EIRA  
Pressure displacement.

Their eyes meet. Recognition.

Nara steps forward and puts the black root on the table.

NARA  
Sea salt is entering Tavra’s western gardens through stone.

Ossa rises.

OSSA  
An unverified plant illness was contained.

NARA  
Contained in a false yield report.

The hall erupts.

A child’s voice cuts through.

KES (O.S.)  
Five.

Kes stands at the entrance with LUMA REED, his mother, elegant in ambassador indigo.

AVEN  
Five what?

KES  
Five warnings. My country drowned.

Luma reaches for him. He steps away.

AVEN  
How many survived?

KES  
Forty-one.

AVEN  
How many lived there?

KES  
Two hundred and sixteen.

A record keeper whispers that no settlement is registered.

Kes says the full marsh name.

The ice in Orun’s bowl CRACKS.

Everyone hears it.

INT. COPPER HALL — NIGHT #12#

The argument has lasted hours.

RUSK  
Western pressure. Reversed lake currents. Salt intrusion. A drowned margin.

OSSA  
Four unrelated events.

EIRA  
No event is unrelated because a council needs it to be.

MARU  
Suun cannot receive uncontrolled migration based on metaphor and rotten roots.

Kes throws a clay map fragment at him. Guards move. Luma blocks them.

LUMA  
Touch him and every marsh household leaves the Accord.

MARU  
How many households is that, Ambassador? Your records never agree.

The cruelty lands.

Ilyon stands.

The room quiets because it loves him.

ILYON  
For sixty days, matched measurements. Orun repairs its western marker. Suun sounds its basin. Tavra tests every spring. Kheled compares moon, well and tide. All findings return to this table.

SIMO  
And public warning?

Ilyon’s hand goes to his copper band.

ILYON  
A warning without instruction is panic wearing virtue.

EIRA  
And silence without certainty is still silence.

Aven considers both.

AVEN  
We measure first.

Rusk calls it a beginning.

Eira looks at the melting ice.

EIRA  
It is already late.

CUT TO:

INT. COPPER HALL PASSAGE — LATER #13#

Ilyon washes his hands. They shake.

Nara enters.

NARA  
You knew Ossa’s report was false.

ILYON  
I knew you disagreed.

NARA  
That is how leaders rename knowledge they don’t want.

Ilyon grips the basin.

ILYON  
When I was nine, a priest said the mountain would bury Tavra before dawn. Everyone ran. Four hundred and twelve people died under each other. The mountain did not erupt.

He looks at his reflection in copper.

ILYON (CONT'D)  
I was found under three bodies.

Nara’s anger softens, but does not disappear.

ILYON (CONT'D)  
I don’t fear warning people. I fear what warning does after it leaves the mouth.

NARA  
I fear what silence does before it leaves one.

EXT. TAVRA TERRACE — NIGHT #14#

Eira stands above the sea, uncomfortable with the warm air.

Seli joins her.

SELI  
Your ocean moves one way at a time. It seems restful.

EIRA  
It has tides.

SELI  
Predictable ones.

She hands Eira the clay navigation disc.

SELI (CONT'D)  
Iron needle. It has pointed north since my grandmother’s grandmother.

The needle TREMBLES. Swings west. Returns north.

EIRA  
When did it begin?

SELI  
After the shore moved.

Eira places the disc on stone. It swings west again.

SELI (CONT'D)  
Is that information?

EIRA  
It is two things being wrong in the same direction.

Below them, Kes maps the drowned village in wet clay. Nara helps him mix earth.

The four leads occupy one frame, not yet knowing they have become a family of circumstance.

INT. ILYON AND BEREN’S HOME — NIGHT #15#

Beren kneads dough. Ilyon stares at evacuation casualty tablets from his childhood.

Simo paces.

SIMO  
Sixty days is surrender.

ILYON  
Sixty days is the vote we had.

SIMO  
Because they didn’t believe her.

ILYON  
Because belief is not a civic plan.

Simo notices Ilyon’s hands shaking.

SIMO  
You still hear that crowd.

Beren stops kneading.

Ilyon looks at his protégé.

ILYON  
Do not use love as a knife.

Simo lowers his eyes.

SIMO  
Forgive me.

He means it. That makes him dangerous.

MONTAGE — THE SIXTY DAYS #16#

— Eira and Seli exchange tablets by courier.

— Nara tastes springs. Each time: clean. Then one: faint salt.

— Nema Vey measures stars and tide from a Kheledi tower.

— Oru reaches Orun’s gate. A clerk makes him wait behind fur traders.

— Maru drives new harbour posts and doubles the chain.

— Tovan Ash-Hand trains rope crews over a blue crevasse. He jokes; no one sees him touch a dead husband’s bead at his throat.

— Kes sleeps in a Tavran storehouse beside his map basket, refusing Luma’s guest bed.

— Ilyon speaks in public. “No evidence of immediate danger.” Simo watches the crowd relax and hates him for succeeding.

— Beneath the western glacier, black water moves.

EXT. ORUN SOUTH GATE — DAY #17#

Words painted in copper: THE ICE REMEMBERS YOUR LIES.

Attendants scrub them into a pink stain.

Delegates arrive for the joint demonstration.

TOVAN, 38, scarred right hand and reckless smile, unloads equipment.

He catches a falling crate one-handed before it crushes Kes.

TOVAN  
If you want to die, choose something people will sing better.

KES  
I wasn’t dying.

TOVAN  
Excellent. My rescue record remains clean.

Eira passes.

TOVAN (CONT'D)  
Listener.

EIRA  
Former Captain.

TOVAN  
Every flirtation with you feels like a disciplinary hearing.

She almost smiles.

INT. FIRST LISTENING VAULT, ORUN — DAY #18#

A hundred witnesses. Four black pillars.

SURA NETH, 62, supervises the instruments. Pell has sealed all music chambers.

Eira addresses the room.

EIRA  
Direct strike at seven breaths. Known returns at eleven, sixteen and twenty-three. The anomalous return at nine.

SIMO  
If it doesn’t come?

EIRA  
We learn it didn’t come.

SIMO  
So your warning survives any outcome.

EIRA  
My uncertainty survives. The claim changes.

Eira pulls the signal cord.

Tower lamps flash.

Everyone touches stone.

STRIKE.

Seven.

Eleven.

Sixteen.

Twenty-three.

No nine.

Whispers.

Eira’s composure strains.

EIRA  
Again.

They reset.

STRIKE.

Seven.

NINE.

The room reacts.

Then a return at TEN — impossibly loud.

The pillar RINGS. Copper lamps shake.

Sura’s face changes.

SURA  
Stop the marker!

Eira runs.

INT. NORTH RESONATOR CHAMBER — CONTINUOUS #19#

She breaks the wax seal and yanks the door open.

A hidden COPPER PLATE vibrates against the wall, connected to the pillar by a thin line.

Pell grabs it, burns his hand.

PELL  
This isn’t mine.

Witnesses crowd the door.

Simo pushes forward, horrified.

The genuine warning has just been murdered by false evidence.

AVEN  
Who had access?

Sura finds a copied seal on the line housing.

Her own.

All eyes turn to her.

SURA  
Copied.

Var slips away at the back.

Eira sees him go.

EXT. ORUN ANIMAL PENS — DAY #20#

Var packs a sled. Eira corners him.

EIRA  
You sold access.

He keeps working.

VAR  
A maintenance passage. Three months ago.

EIRA  
To whom?

VAR  
I never met them.

EIRA  
Whose copper?

VAR  
Tavran.

She grabs his coat.

EIRA  
The false note makes every true one worthless.

VAR  
I know.

EIRA  
Then give me a name.

VAR  
A buyer’s silence is the only thing a trader sells once.

EIRA  
Mother died on a route opened with my copied seal.

Var goes still.

EIRA (CONT'D)  
You know what a false mark costs.

VAR  
I was sixteen.

EIRA  
She is still dead.

Var looks at her, guilt naked now.

VAR  
You did hear the nine, didn’t you? Before the plate?

EIRA  
Yes.

VAR  
Will anyone believe you?

She cannot answer.

INT. GUEST HOUSE, ORUN — NIGHT #21#

Tiri, 10, thin and watchful, steals Aven’s coat from a warming room.

Inside a sewn pocket, she finds a secret evacuation map: sled capacities, food loads, an eastern route.

She crawls through a vent and drops into darkness beside Kes.

TIRI  
Who are you?

KES  
Do you have food?

She gives him a stolen salt sweet.

He studies the map.

KES (CONT'D)  
This isn’t treasure. It’s evacuation.

TIRI  
Orun doesn’t evacuate.

KES  
Then why count sleds?

They hear Aven and Rusk arguing through the wall.

AVEN (O.S.)  
A plan causes no flood. The absence of one causes deaths.

RUSK (O.S.)  
If that map circulates, the roads fill before stores do.

Tiri folds the bark into the secret pocket of her second coat.

INT. ORUN COUNCIL CHAMBER — NIGHT #22#

Chaos.

Simo accuses Orun of fabricating crisis for stores. Varo, a beautiful seer, accuses Eira of sacrilege. Suun threatens to withdraw.

Ilyon stands silent.

Eira enters.

EIRA  
Someone used Tavran copper and a copied Oruni seal.

All eyes find Ilyon.

ILYON  
Tavra will open every delegation record.

SIMO  
Convenient. The accused searches itself.

RUSK  
Until inquiry concludes, Orun issues no public warning.

EIRA  
You are punishing the warning for being attacked.

RUSK  
I am preventing a city from tearing itself apart.

EIRA  
The shelf doesn’t care whether we remain civil.

Rusk’s calm cracks.

RUSK  
I was there for Tavra’s false evacuation. I watched a mother suffocate her child against a gate. Do not lecture me about the cost of fear.

EIRA  
Then stop making fear the only thing you measure.

She leaves.

EXT. ORUN ROOF — NIGHT #23#

Eira stands alone under aurora.

Tovan joins her with two cups.

TOVAN  
Var’s recipe. Possibly illegal.

She refuses.

TOVAN (CONT'D)  
Good. More for the disgraced.

EIRA  
You enjoy being disgraced.

TOVAN  
It saves time disappointing people.

A beat.

EIRA  
The note was real.

TOVAN  
I believe you.

She turns sharply.

EIRA  
Why?

TOVAN  
You look miserable. Liars usually enjoy being believed.

She almost laughs, then doesn’t.

TOVAN (CONT'D)  
The old station may still hold records.

EIRA  
It’s beyond the fracture field.

TOVAN  
Yes.

EIRA  
You were demoted for taking an unauthorized team beyond a fracture field.

TOVAN  
Different field.

EIRA  
Your husband died.

His smile remains. Everything behind it changes.

TOVAN  
Also different.

Below, a gate alarm sounds.

Oru has arrived with Korun’s lion tracks.

The animals are all moving east.

INT. STORE TUNNEL — NIGHT #24#

Var follows a hooded figure.

VAR  
I know you ordered the copper.

The figure turns: SIMO.

He looks sick, not sinister.

SIMO  
I ordered a resonance. One clean echo. Enough to make them act.

VAR  
You attached a second plate.

SIMO  
No.

VAR  
Someone did.

Simo realizes.

A SHADOW moves behind Var.

Var turns — struck hard.

He falls. The hooded attacker drags Simo into darkness.

Var sees only a copper ring engraved with a mountain.

Then the attacker kicks him unconscious.

CUT TO BLACK.

=== ACT TWO ===

INT. HEALING CAVE — MORNING #25#

Deya Flint stitches Var’s scalp.

Eira, Tovan, Seli, Nara and Aven stand around him.

VAR  
Simo ordered the first plate. He says not the second.

AVEN  
Why believe him?

VAR  
Because he was more frightened than I was.

NARA  
Who took him?

VAR  
Mountain ring.

Ilyon enters.

He wears such a ring.

Silence.

He removes it and places it on the table.

ILYON  
Every member of Tavra’s eruption guard wears one.

EIRA  
How many came to Orun?

ILYON  
Twelve.

TOVAN  
Then we only need to distrust twelve people. A restful morning.

EIRA  
The station records settle this.

AVEN  
If they exist.

EIRA  
If they don’t, we learn they don’t.

Tovan smiles.

TOVAN  
I knew I liked her.

EXT. WESTERN SHELF — DAY #26#

A rescue expedition crosses blue-white immensity:

Eira. Tovan. Seli. Nara. Aven. Korun. Nemi, the young sledwright. Six rope crew.

Aven ordered Nara to join because salt may identify subterranean sea contact. Seli carries magnetic discs. They spin unpredictably.

Wind erases their trail behind them.

SELI  
On water, a route moves after you pass.

EIRA  
Here it disappears.

SELI  
That is moving with better manners.

Ahead, cave lion tracks cross the route — east.

Korun studies them.

KORUN  
They ran here.

Mammoths walk. Lions run.

A SHARP CRACK.

The ice beneath Nara drops.

Tovan dives, catches her wrist with his burned hand — it slips. He catches with the other as a blue crevasse opens under her.

Seli and Eira anchor the rope.

They pull Nara out.

She lies gasping.

TOVAN  
Are you alive?

NARA  
Temporarily.

TOVAN  
Best kind.

Nara looks into the crack.

Far below, BLACK WATER moves beneath the ice.

INT. TAVRA ERUPTION GUARD QUARTERS — DAY #27#

Ilyon and Maru search bunks.

They find Simo’s notes hidden beneath a mat: crowd-flow diagrams, projected deaths, copies of Eira’s report.

Beren arrives with a guard roster.

BEREN  
One mountain ring unaccounted for. Dar Olt.

ILYON  
Commander of the sea wall?

BEREN  
He left Orun last night. Alone.

Maru finds a line in Simo’s notes: A FALSE CERTAINTY MAY SERVE A TRUE DANGER.

MARU  
Your student.

ILYON  
My failure.

MARU  
Do not make responsibility poetic. It wastes time.

EXT. WESTERN FRACTURE FIELD — DUSK #28#

The expedition reaches a new crevasse.

Fifty arm-lengths below sits the missing listening station, whole, tilted on an ice shelf.

A lamp glows inside.

NEMI  
Tell me that’s reflected sun.

TOVAN  
Sun’s behind us.

NEMI  
Luminous worm?

TOVAN  
Lamp.

They rig Nemi’s broad sled as anchor.

EIRA  
We return with a vault team.

TOVAN  
Seven days.

EIRA  
The station has been missing months.

TOVAN  
Then seven matter greatly to anyone alive.

Eira sees it: his need.

EIRA  
You don’t rescue people. You ask them to participate in rescuing you.

The words hit.

Tovan looks down at the lamp.

TOVAN  
Maybe. Tie the second anchor anyway.

INT. FALLEN LISTENING STATION — NIGHT #29#

Tovan and Eira descend.

Inside: four keepers, dead in arranged positions. Edda Mor sits beneath the lamp with tablets in her lap.

Eira kneels before her.

The clay is filled with shrinking time intervals.

Water ROARS below.

EIRA  
This isn’t a cavity.

Nara’s voice from the roof.

NARA (O.S.)  
The air tastes of sea salt.

The station SHIFTS.

Black water bursts through the floor.

Eira straps tablets to her chest. Tovan tries to lift Edda’s body.

EIRA  
Leave her.

TOVAN  
We don’t leave people.

EIRA  
She is dead.

He freezes.

Peleth’s voice in memory: *Stop digging.*

Tovan takes Edda’s final tablet instead.

They climb onto the roof as the building rolls.

TOVAN  
PULL!

The team hauls Eira up. The station drops away under Tovan.

His rope catches. He slams into blue ice.

Below, the station sinks through black water, lamp glowing like a falling star.

Tovan’s burned hand loses grip.

Eira, hanging above, reaches down.

EIRA  
Take my hand!

TOVAN  
Poor rescue procedure!

EIRA  
Take it!

He does.

Together the team drags them over the lip as the crevasse closes with a deafening BOOM.

INT. ICE CAVE CAMP — NIGHT #30#

Storm traps the expedition.

Eira arranges tablets. Seli translates intervals into water movement. Nara maps salinity. Separate knowledge becomes one picture.

A vast body of water lies behind the western shelf — an inland ocean held above inhabited valleys.

SELI  
My lake isn’t folding on its own. Something is pressing from north to south.

NARA  
And forcing the sea through Tavra’s rock.

EIRA  
The ice dam is failing.

NEMI  
How long?

Eira turns Edda’s last tablet over.

Ordinary writing:

THE WATER IS NOT TRAPPED BENEATH THE ICE. THE ICE IS TRAPPED ABOVE THE WATER.

A low note moves through the cave.

Snow falls from the ceiling.

EIRA  
Less than sixty days.

A FIGURE appears at the cave entrance.

Simo, half-frozen, blood on his face.

Behind him — COMMANDER DAR OLT with a stone blade at his throat.

DAR  
Give me the tablets.

Tovan slowly rises.

TOVAN  
You travelled far for reading material.

DAR  
Tavra’s sea wall was built on the Accord’s promise that Orun maintained the shelf. If these records spread, the coast riots before we can seal the gates.

NARA  
The sea is already inside the roots.

DAR  
Then we need order more than truth.

Simo looks at Eira.

SIMO  
I made the first echo. I thought—

EIRA  
You thought truth needed your help.

SIMO  
I was right about the danger.

EIRA  
And now no one will believe it.

Dar tightens the blade.

DAR  
Tablets.

Eira looks at Tovan. At Seli. Nara.

She slides the stack forward.

Dar reaches.

Nemi KICKS the lamp out.

Darkness.

ACTION IN SOUND:

A grunt. Blade scrapes stone. Tovan hits someone. Simo cries out.

Eira feels for tablets — hands one to Seli, one to Nara, one to Nemi.

The lamp relights.

Dar has Tovan against the wall. Simo bleeds on the floor.

Korun stands behind Dar with a bow drawn.

KORUN  
Lions left because they are wiser than cities.

DAR  
Then go live with lions.

KORUN  
I have considered it.

Dar releases Tovan.

A RUMBLE grows.

The cave floor splits between them. Water erupts upward.

Dar falls across the crack. Tovan catches him.

For a moment Dar hangs above black water, held by the man he threatened.

DAR  
Why?

TOVAN  
It’s an illness.

They pull him up.

The mountain shifts. The exit begins collapsing.

EIRA  
MOVE!

They flee into the storm.

EXT. WESTERN SHELF — NIGHT #31#

Whiteout.

The team follows a single rope. One hand to rope, one to the person ahead.

Simo stumbles. Nara supports him.

SIMO  
You should let me fall.

NARA  
That would make your guilt very convenient.

Behind them, Dar looks back.

In the storm, a distant chain of orange lights moves west toward the sea wall — Dar’s guard patrol.

He makes a decision.

DAR  
They will arrest you at Orun.

AVEN  
On whose authority?

DAR  
Mine.

He takes off his mountain ring and gives it to Korun.

DAR (CONT'D)  
Ride ahead. Tell them the commander orders the gates opened to these witnesses.

SIMO  
You tried to bury the evidence.

DAR  
And failed. I try not to repeat engineering mistakes.

The rope snaps taut.

A fissure races beneath their feet.

RUNNING now — tied together — as the glacier splits behind them.

Nemi’s broad sled jumps a gap. Nara falls. Seli catches her. Tovan cuts a dragging cargo line before it pulls everyone in.

The tablet crate disappears into blue darkness.

Eira watches it go.

EIRA  
We lost the records.

Seli opens her coat. One tablet.

Nara: another. Nemi: another. Simo: another.

They distributed the truth.

INT. ORUN COUNCIL CHAMBER — DAY #32#

Eira places Edda’s final tablet on the copper table.

The returned expedition stands bruised and frostbitten.

Rusk reads the warning.

RUSK  
How long?

EIRA  
Nine to forty days.

The room reacts.

AVEN  
Your confidence?

EIRA  
That is the range.

RUSK  
And the city?

TOVAN  
Twenty-three thousand can take the south road before day nine if they leave tonight.

RUSK  
Orun holds forty-six thousand.

Silence.

NEMI  
My broad runners can cross wet ice. We build them as boats.

HADRAN VO, the old sled master, bristles.

HADRAN  
Unseasoned frames twist. Broad runners shear on rock.

NEMI  
Narrow runners sink in water.

HADRAN  
They are sleds.

NEMI  
Not anymore.

Aven turns to Rusk.

AVEN  
Order evacuation.

He cannot.

RUSK  
The false warning killed confidence. If we announce nine days, half the city runs without food.

Eira sees it clearly: Rusk is not corrupt. He is terrified.

EIRA  
Then don’t announce nine days. Announce a road. A ration. A name for the first household to leave. Give fear a task.

Rusk looks at her.

This is not how Eira used to speak.

EXT. ORUN — CONTINUOUS #33#

Black doors open across the city.

A great HORN sounds three times.

People stop in markets, vaults, baths, workshops.

Rusk’s voice carries through stone speaking tubes.

RUSK (V.O.)  
The western shelf is unstable. South Hearth departs at sunset. River Hearth follows at moonrise. Carry seven days of food. One memory object. No household travels alone.

A beat.

Then Orun moves.

— Nemi takes command of every sled shop.

— Hadran watches workers adopt her broad design.

— Iso Wren drains sacred lamp oil into waterproofing vats.

— Ama Kel unlocks the forbidden name-caves to create a passage through the ridge.

— Pell opens the city’s resonators.

PELL  
If the ice moves, every wall will sound.

— Varo the seer gathers followers separately.

VARO  
The faithful remain. Orun was promised to the ice.

INT. LISTENING VAULT — DAY #34#

Eira finds Pell retuning a copper plate.

EIRA  
You’re staying.

PELL  
The alarm requires someone to open the chambers in sequence.

EIRA  
A child can pull a lever.

PELL  
Then a child should leave.

She sees what he intends.

EIRA  
I lost Mother because Var forged my seal. I let myself believe it was my calibration because guilt was simpler than hating him.

Pell stops.

PELL  
I knew.

The words hit harder than a confession.

EIRA  
You knew?

PELL  
Not then. Later. He told me.

EIRA  
And you let me carry it.

PELL  
I was afraid if I gave you someone to blame, I would lose both of you.

EIRA  
So you chose which child to bury.

She walks out.

Pell stands alone with the instrument.

EXT. LAKE ARUUN — DAY #35#

Seli returns to chaos.

Thousands crowd Suun’s floating harbours. Boats are lashed into vast rafts. Maru’s chain remains across the eastern entrance.

Tem embraces Seli, then sees the authority in her face and releases her.

TEM  
I told the council about your model.

SELI  
As yours?

TEM  
As ours.

SELI  
There is no ours when only your name opens the door.

She addresses the NAVIGATORS.

SELI (CONT'D)  
The northern basin will empty south. All inherited routes are dead. We cross the reed shallows east, then climb the drowned river.

Murmurs. Tem studies her chart.

TEM  
The east shallows cannot carry cargo hulls.

SELI  
At current water. When the lake steps back, they become roads.

Kiri Drenn, old and drifting, sings nearby.

KIRI  
The lake steps backward to gather its long skirts.

Seli looks at her.

SELI  
And then?

Kiri becomes lucid.

KIRI  
It runs.

Maru approaches.

MARU  
Eastern harbour remains closed to unregistered craft.

Kes, beside Seli, stares at him.

SELI  
There will be no harbour.

MARU  
There will be if people follow capacity.

KES  
Your capacity has names.

Maru cannot meet his eyes.

INT. COPPER HALL, TAVRA — DAY #36#

Ilyon addresses a packed city.

Simo stands under guard beside him.

ILYON  
The first false echo was commissioned by my protégé.

Crowd fury.

SIMO  
I acted alone.

Ilyon turns to him.

ILYON  
No. You acted inside a silence I created.

The crowd quiets.

ILYON (CONT'D)  
I delayed warning because I feared panic. I called uncertainty responsibility. I allowed false yield reports. I told you there was no immediate danger when I knew danger had not agreed to our language.

Beren watches, proud and heartbroken.

ILYON (CONT'D)  
The coast will flood. We open the mountain caverns. Lower terraces leave now. Every civic family surrenders its reserved place.

A noble shouts.

NOBLE  
On whose authority?

Ilyon removes his copper band.

ILYON  
On the last authority I deserve.

He drops it on the table.

MONTAGE — NINE DAYS #37#

SUPER: DAY NINE

— Nara stands before two seed vaults: rare ceremonial plants, common food cuttings. She opens the common vault.

— Mele steals medicine from the elite stores and redistributes it. Nara sees, helps load the basket.

— Sava Ink-Palm chooses records for one sled, then watches children play a stone game not represented anywhere in the archive.

— Tarek orders Kheled’s sacred cisterns opened as overflow chambers.

— Aven faces the moon court.

AVEN  
Evacuation compulsory.

The vote ties.

All look at her.

She remembers the old water dispute. Her deadly delay.

AVEN (CONT'D)  
Yes.

The court moves.

SUPER: DAY SEVEN

— Oru guides Roadless wagons toward the eastern pass. Mammoths ahead.

— Korun marks their route for Oruni refugees.

— Tovan strings rope across a ravine.

— Var opens smuggler tunnels for families excluded from official lists.

— Olan the clerk writes four hundred migrants into existence as FIFTH HEARTH.

SUPER: DAY FIVE

— Lake Aruun drops a handspan.

— Tavra’s volcano exhales ash. Day turns copper-black.

— Nema watches the stars disappear.

— Eira’s instruments show intervals collapsing.

SUPER: DAY THREE

— People on the exposed lakebed gather stranded fish.

Seli screams through a cone.

SELI  
GET OFF THE LAKE!

They ignore her.

— Varo leads thousands back toward Orun.

— Pell’s alarm levers wait.

SUPER: DAY ONE

Absolute silence.

No insects. No birds. No wind.

The horizon west of Orun seems slightly higher.

INT. ORUN THIRD VAULT — NIGHT #38#

Eira sits where the story began.

The strike comes without her signal.

One breath.

Return.

One breath.

Return.

The glacier no longer contains distance.

Pell enters.

PELL  
The last households are in the name passage.

EIRA  
Come with me.

PELL  
The west and north chambers must open together.

EIRA  
I don’t forgive you.

PELL  
I know.

EIRA  
You don’t get to die and turn that into forgiveness.

PELL  
I am not dying for forgiveness.

He touches the listening pillar.

PELL (CONT'D)  
I am staying because this city needs one final note, and because I am the person here.

Eira’s eyes fill. She hates him for making sense.

Pell gives her the small stone striker that belonged to her mother.

PELL (CONT'D)  
Your mother believed measurement could save people. I believed beauty could. We were both vain.

EIRA  
What saves them?

PELL  
People. If they move now.

A pressure wave hits.

Every lamp goes out.

Pell pulls the first lever.

EXT. ORUN — NIGHT #39#

The entire city becomes a bell.

A LOW TONE explodes from walls, streets, floors.

People scream and move.

Pell runs through resonator tunnels opening chamber after chamber.

WEST. NORTH. RIVER. EAST.

Each adds a note. The alarm becomes music vast enough to shake snow from roofs.

Eira reaches the south gate with Tovan.

Behind them, the horizon RISES.

Not a wave.

The western ice shelf lifting as black water forces itself beneath.

EIRA  
Run.

=== ACT THREE ===

EXT. WESTERN SHELF — CONTINUOUS #40#

The glacier breaks.

A line races across the plain faster than horses. Ice slabs tilt into the air. Black water punches through in towers.

Orun’s outer listening towers vanish.

The released glacial lake becomes a moving wall filled with icebergs, stone and forest torn from valleys unseen.

EXT. SOUTH ROAD, ORUN — NIGHT #41#

Forty thousand people choke the road.

Nemi’s broad sled-boats skim flooded ice. Hadran directs launches, abandoning every traditional rule with increasing enthusiasm.

HADRAN  
Wider! Make the cursed things wider!

Tiri, wearing two coats, pulls Kes onto a sled.

Var finds Eira.

VAR  
Father?

She looks back at the sounding city.

No answer needed.

Var folds in half. Eira grabs his coat.

EIRA  
You grieve while moving.

It is something Sura once told her.

They move.

A section of road COLLAPSES, leaving a torrent-filled gap.

Tovan’s rope crossing is the only path.

TOVAN  
One hand to rope! Children inside! No carts!

A noble family refuses to abandon a loaded sled.

Tovan cuts its harness. Memory objects spill into water.

NOBLE  
That is our history!

TOVAN  
Then remember it!

INT. RESONATOR TUNNEL — NIGHT #42#

Water bursts through Pell’s final chamber.

He reaches the river lever.

Through stone, he hears the foot rhythm from his concert — thousands now running over the south road.

Pell smiles.

He opens the chamber.

The last note carries through Orun as water takes him.

EXT. ROPE CROSSING — NIGHT #43#

The flood reaches the ravine.

People crawl across three ropes above churning ice water.

Tovan stands on the failing Orun side, fastening harnesses.

Eira crosses, then realizes he is not attached.

EIRA  
Your line!

TOVAN  
Anchor’s cracked. Someone has to hold the brake.

EIRA  
We can secure from this side.

He looks at the final crowd: thirty people. Maybe time for twenty.

TOVAN  
No.

Eira starts back.

Tovan draws his knife and cuts her return line.

EIRA  
Tovan!

TOVAN  
You were right about me.

He fastens a child’s mitten.

TOVAN (CONT'D)  
I kept making people watch me save them.

He sends the child across.

TOVAN (CONT'D)  
Look away.

Eira does not.

Tovan holds the brake as person after person crosses.

The anchor tears halfway out.

Last is Varo, the seer, dragging a terrified follower.

VARO  
The ice was promised to us.

TOVAN  
Promises change under pressure.

He shoves them onto the rope.

The flood hits.

Tovan disappears in black water and blue ice.

On the far side, Eira makes no sound.

The blast of pressure ruptures her eardrums.

The world goes SILENT.

EXT. LAKE ARUUN — DAWN #44#

Silence continues from Eira’s perspective over images elsewhere.

The inland sea withdraws.

Miles of lakebed emerge. Boats settle into mud. Fish thrash under a red dawn.

Then sound SLAMS BACK as we leave Eira.

Seli stands on a grounded boat.

A dark line appears across the northern horizon.

SELI  
It’s running.

She raises a red sail.

Across the armada, red sails rise.

SELI (CONT'D)  
Cut every harbour line! East channel! Follow the reeds!

Tem sees families still on the exposed lakebed.

TEM  
We can take fifty more.

SELI  
The first surge reaches us in twelve hundred breaths.

TEM  
Then count slowly.

He turns his boat toward the stranded.

Seli blocks him.

SELI  
You stole my work because you said people would only follow your name.

TEM  
They are following it now.

SELI  
Not there.

He touches her face.

TEM  
I was proud of you in a way that left no room for you.

He turns away before forgiveness can simplify it.

His boat races toward the lakebed.

EXT. EASTERN HARBOUR — CONTINUOUS #45#

Maru’s great chain blocks unregistered craft from the exit.

Refugee boats crush against it.

Renn Drenn hacks at a link.

RENN  
Open it!

MARU  
The release is jammed.

Kes arrives in a small marsh canoe with children.

Maru sees him.

Behind them, the dark horizon grows.

Maru looks at the harbour he spent his life building.

He gives Renn an axe.

MARU (CONT'D)  
Not the chain. The posts.

They chop the massive reed-and-timber harbour apart.

Maru’s orderly world collapses by his own hand. Freed beams become rafts. Kes directs them through channels only marsh people know.

KES  
Not there! Mint water is deep. Follow the yellow reeds!

Maru obeys an eleven-year-old.

The surge enters the harbour.

Boats rise like leaves.

EXT. LAKEBED — CONTINUOUS #46#

Tem loads the last stranded family.

The surge is upon them.

His heavy boat cannot turn in mud.

Seli’s armada passes along the eastern channel.

Tem sees her red sail.

He gives the steering oar to a young passenger.

TEM  
When the stern lifts, point between those reeds. Do not fight the first current. It is stronger and stupid. Use the second.

PASSENGER  
And you?

Tem jumps into the mud and pushes.

The boat slides free.

Water consumes him.

Seli sees from a distance.

She does not get to stop.

INT. TAVRA MIRROR GARDENS — DAY #47#

Ash turns daylight red.

Nara, Mele and Beren load children and seed cuttings into cavern lifts.

Salt water jets from cracks in the walls.

Ossa stands at the main feeder controls.

NARA  
Leave it.

OSSA  
If I close the upper gate, it buys the lower terraces time.

MELE  
You told us the gardens were healthy.

OSSA  
Yes.

MELE  
People died believing you.

OSSA  
Yes.

No defence. It confuses Mele more than denial.

Ossa gives Nara the complete water map.

OSSA (CONT'D)  
I moved Red Spring three years ago. The soil was failing. I thought one good harvest would give me time to repair it.

NARA  
Time for whom?

Ossa looks at the city she loved badly.

OSSA  
Everyone. That is how I excused it.

She closes the upper gate. A stone wheel locks.

OSSA (CONT'D)  
Go.

Nara and Mele leave with the children.

The wall ruptures.

Mineral water and ash take Ossa and the orange terraces.

EXT. TAVRA SEA WALL — DAY #48#

The ocean pulls away from the coast.

Fish and kelp lie exposed below black cliffs.

Dar stands at the wall controls with Ilyon.

The city behind them climbs toward caverns.

A white line forms at sea.

DAR  
The wall can take one wave.

ILYON  
And the second?

DAR  
It was designed by optimistic ancestors.

If they keep gates closed, reflected pressure will climb the residential terraces. If they open them, the harbour and wall crews die.

Dar hands Ilyon the speaking cone.

DAR (CONT'D)  
Tell them the truth.

Ilyon’s old terror returns: crushing crowd, lost hand, bodies.

He climbs the wall.

ILYON  
People of Tavra.

His voice carries by copper reflectors.

The city looks up.

ILYON (CONT'D)  
The first wave will break the harbour. The second will reach the lower ovens. The western cavern remains open for thirty-two hundred more. Do not run. Take the hand of the person behind you. Move at the drum.

Jori Flint-Eye begins a steady rhythm in the tunnels.

Thousands step together.

Not panic. Choreography.

Ilyon looks at Dar.

ILYON (CONT'D)  
Come with us.

DAR  
The gates open from here.

ILYON  
There must be another way.

DAR  
That sentence built half our monuments.

The wave grows.

Dar smiles faintly.

DAR (CONT'D)  
I wrote poems about the sea.

ILYON  
Were they good?

DAR  
No.

He throws the gate levers.

The harbour opens.

The first wave hits.

Dar and the sea wall vanish in white violence.

Pressure floods the empty harbour instead of the climbing city.

INT. TAVRA EVACUATION TUNNEL — CONTINUOUS #49#

People move to Jori’s drum.

Ilyon enters, soaked and injured.

Beren reaches him.

For a moment they hold each other.

A CHILD falls. The rhythm stutters. Crowd compresses.

Ilyon’s trauma consumes him — bodies, screaming, no air.

Beren takes his face.

BEREN  
This crowd is not that crowd.

Ilyon breathes.

He lifts the child and starts the count.

ILYON  
One step. One breath. One step. One breath.

The crowd repeats it.

Movement resumes.

EXT. KHELED MOON COURT — NIGHT #50#

Floodwater arrives across the Sunward Plain as a shining wall under stars.

People crowd the roofless court.

Tarek stands at the cistern controls. Aven beside him.

TAREK  
If we open overflow chambers, every drinking cistern contaminates.

AVEN  
If we don’t?

TAREK  
The lower city takes the full force.

Aven looks at thousands waiting for her to consider another side.

AVEN  
Open them.

TAREK  
The court must approve—

AVEN  
Open them.

He does.

Ancient channels ROAR. Floodwater pours into sacred wells, absorbing the first surge.

The court floor cracks. People scream.

AVEN (CONT'D)  
East stair! Leave everything!

A noble clutches a painted legal history.

SAVA takes it from him and throws it into water.

NOBLE  
That is six hundred years!

Sava gives him a blank tablet.

SAVA  
Then live and write seven hundred.

The archive wall COLLAPSES. A cart of old records overturns toward the water.

Sava does not reach for them.

She lifts a small box of blank clay and shoves it into Aven's arms.

SAVA (CONT'D)  
Leave room for what happens next.

A second surge tears through the court. Tarek catches Aven. Sava is swept behind a falling limestone screen.

Aven starts back.

Through a gap, Sava meets her eyes and shakes her head.

The screen disappears under black water.

Aven clutches the blank tablets and leads the living uphill.

EXT. EASTERN PASS — DAWN #51#

The four evacuations converge in chaos.

Oruni sled-boats. Suun reed craft dragged over mud. Tavran cavern survivors black with ash. Kheledi families in wet white linen. Roadless wagons and mammoths above them.

No common authority.

A bottleneck forms at a narrow stone pass.

Maru orders boats first. Rusk orders frostbitten Oruni first. Kheledi guards defend their cistern carts. Fighting begins.

Kes climbs a wagon.

He holds up the broken clay map of his drowned village.

No one listens.

Mara-of-No-Hearth takes Jori’s drum and strikes once.

The sound carries.

She points to Kes.

MARA  
The first country drowned before any of yours. Hear its speaker.

Kes looks over the terrain.

KES  
This was a marsh before it was dry. The centre path is old mud. It will swallow carts. Boats there. Sleds on the stone edge. Walkers through the yellow grass.

Bel Aru’s ground hornbills rise from the yellow grass and land beyond the pass.

Oru nods.

ORU  
Child and birds agree. Better council than most.

Rusk cedes command first.

RUSK  
Do it.

The cultures reorganize together.

Civilization survives its first minute as something new.

EXT. EASTERN PASS — LATER #52#

The final surge reaches them.

A sled overturns. Tiri is trapped beneath it. Kes tries to lift the frame.

Eira, deaf, sees but cannot hear them.

She runs back. Var and Nemi join.

They free Tiri. An infant nearby turns blue with cold.

Tiri clutches her second coat. The secret evacuation map is sewn inside.

She looks at the infant.

Then gives up the coat.

The map goes with it.

The written plan dissolves in rain while the people it helped save carry one another uphill.

EXT. HIGH RIDGE — SUNSET #53#

Survivors watch the old world drown.

Orun is gone beneath a broken inland sea.

Lake Aruun has become a torn river valley.

Tavra burns behind white surf.

Kheled’s moon courts stand as islands.

Eira hears nothing.

Nara sits beside her. She does not speak. She places Eira’s hand on the ground.

Through stone, faint vibrations: thousands of survivors breathing, moving, crying.

Eira feels them.

Var kneels nearby.

VAR  
Eira.

She cannot hear.

He touches his throat, then the clay tablet: *I am sorry.*

Eira takes the stylus.

Writes: *Sorry is the beginning of a road.*

She does not write where it ends.

EXT. REFUGEE CAMP — FIRST MORNING #54#

No one slept.

The horizon has changed.

People wait for water to recede.

It does not.

Nara opens her bundle. Most cuttings are crushed. One bitter-orange stem remains alive.

Kes watches her press it into foreign soil.

KES  
Will it grow here?

NARA  
I don’t know.

KES  
You’re a gardener.

NARA  
That is why I know I don’t know.

He helps pack earth around it.

Seli sits at the water’s edge, holding Tem’s red navigation cord. Maru approaches.

MARU  
Your route saved twelve thousand.

SELI  
My father’s route killed him.

MARU  
Both are true.

SELI  
I don’t need you to mediate my grief.

MARU  
No.

He sits at a respectful distance.

For once, he closes nothing.

INT. MAKESHIFT COUNCIL TENT — DAY #55#

Surviving leaders face an angry crowd.

Rusk. Ilyon. Aven. Maru. Nema. Simo under guard.

Calls for judgment.

SURVIVOR  
Who knew?

No one answers quickly.

Eira enters. Deya has bound her ears. Mara interprets Eira’s signs and written words.

EIRA / MARA  
I knew first that something was wrong. Not what. Not when.

Rusk stands.

RUSK  
I suppressed her first report.

ILYON  
I delayed public warning.

AVEN  
I chose more evidence over more time.

MARU  
I closed the harbour.

SIMO  
I falsified the echo.

The crowd wants one body to hold all blame.

Simo steps forward.

SIMO (CONT'D)  
Take mine.

Eira signs sharply.

EIRA / MARA  
No.

Everyone looks at her.

EIRA / MARA (CONT'D)  
A simple villain is another false certainty.

Simo weeps.

EIRA / MARA (CONT'D)  
He will live and repair what his fear broke.

Some reject this. Some accept. There is no clean catharsis.

Aven rises.

AVEN  
Then judgment begins with work. Water. Shelter. The missing. We can hate each other after sunset.

It is the first good decision she makes without arguing both sides.

EXT. CAMP — DAYS LATER #56#

A new society takes shape.

— Nemi and Hadran build amphibious sled-boats together.

— Tarek filters contaminated water through charcoal and reed beds.

— Nara and Mele plant common food before ceremonial seed.

— Omi establishes shell-call intervals in fog.

— Deya runs a clinic where four healing traditions argue and learn.

— Olan records the Fifth Hearth as equal citizens.

— Maru carries timber under Kes’s direction.

— Ilyon serves bread in Beren’s oven line. No copper band.

— Aven digs latrines beside people she once addressed from courts.

— Eira draws faces because she cannot record their voices.

EXT. STONE BASIN — ONE YEAR LATER — DUSK #57#

A settlement stands on the ridge.

Rough, crowded, alive.

Survivors approach a stone basin carrying small cups of water from wherever they now live.

Oruni snowmelt. Tavran spring. Suun lake water. Kheledi cistern water. Marsh water gathered between yellow reeds.

They pour them together.

Ama Kel begins the Oruni song of names.

Nalo adds a Suun hull rhythm. Jori’s students strike the earth. Kesh the rain caller speaks only the weather.

Mara stands before the people.

MARA  
Tell me what happened.

Voices answer.

ORUNI WOMAN  
An ice beast broke its chain.

SUUN ELDER  
The lake gathered its skirts and ran.

TAVRAN CHILD  
The sea came through the roots.

KHELEDI MAN  
We argued until water made the decision.

ROADLESS GIRL  
The mammoths told us first.

KES  
My country drowned and they said it was empty.

Mara does not choose among them.

MARA  
Good. Again.

They repeat the stories. Already changing.

Luma arrives at the edge of the gathering.

Kes sees his mother.

A year of imagined reunion disappears.

She kneels, not touching him.

LUMA  
I kept asking cities to say your home existed.

KES  
I needed you to come home to it.

LUMA  
I know.

She does not ask forgiveness.

Kes gives her a blank clay tablet.

KES  
Start with the name.

She does.

EXT. BITTER-ORANGE TREE — SUNSET #58#

The cutting has taken root.

Small. Bent by wind. Alive.

Eira sits beneath it with Sava’s final blank tablet.

Around her are the survivors from every part of the story.

She watches their mouths shape different versions of the old world.

Nara sits beside her. Seli. Kes. Ilyon and Beren, together but changed. Aven. Maru. Oru. Mara. Var.

Spaces remain for Tovan, Pell, Tem, Dar, Ossa, Sava and thousands unnamed.

Eira draws the horizon.

Not where it is.

Where they remember it.

Mara looks over her shoulder.

MARA  
Which version is true?

Eira signs.

Mara translates softly.

MARA (CONT'D)  
All of them are too small.

A child touches the basin water.

Ripples cross the reflected sky.

EIRA (V.O.)  
Before it became a legend, the end of the world happened to everyone differently.

The LOW NOTE returns.

But now it is human voices humming together.

FADE OUT.

> THE END <
